            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">

		<tr><td class="subhead">FORTE Science Communications</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.forte-science.co.jp" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.forte-science.co.jp</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">FORTE Science Communications is a socially aware company providing  translation and rewriting services to doctors, scientists and  engineers in the academic and corporate sectors. Our mission, in  part, is to help build bridges of understand between members of the  science commmunity by providing pro bono translation and rewriting services to selected nonprofit, civic and humanitarian organisations working in the service of the public welfare.</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">TILCEPA - Theme on Indigenous and Local Communities, Equity, and Protected Areas</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.iucn.org/themes/ceesp/Wkg_grp/TILCEPA/TILCEPA.htm" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.iucn.org/themes/ceesp/Wkg_grp/TILCEPA/TILCEPA.htm</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The World Commission on Protected Areas (WCPA) and the Commission on Environmental, Economic and Social Policy (CEESP) have agreed to work together on a Theme on Indigenous and Local Communities, Equity, and Protected Areas (TILCEPA). The website gives us a comprehensive view about TILCEPA.</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Periyar Tiger Reserve</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.periyartigerreserve.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.periyartigerreserve.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Dedicated to the Periyar Tiger Reserve in Kerala, this website is managed by the Ecodevelopment Committee of Periyar and includes comprehensive information on the reserve. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Centre for Indian Knowledge Systems</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.ciks.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.ciks.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Centre for Indian Knowledge Systems is devoted to exploring and developing the contemporary relevance and applications of traditional Indian knowledge systems - with a focus on agriculture and health care. 

</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">People for Animals</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.peopleforanimals.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.peopleforanimals.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">People for Animals was founded by Pritish Nandy and Maneka Gandhi, as a people's movement to stop cruelty towards animals and spread the message of ahimsa. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Indiatravelogue</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.indiatravelogue.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.indiatravelogue.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Indiatravelogue is an excellent travel site that provides information on destinations, special deals and holiday packages, besides reviews, interviews and a photo gallery. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">EnvironmentAwards.net</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.environmentawards.net" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.environmentawards.net</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">EnvironmentAwards.net provides a focal point for sponsors, organisers and entrants of environmental and sustainable development awards. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Southern Birdwing</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.southernbirdwing.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.southernbirdwing.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Southern Birdwing is an enterprise started by Goan wildlife enthusiasts Harvey D'Souza and Neil Alvares in October 1997, who help create awareness through educational excursions, talks and workshops. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Traveljini</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.traveljini.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.traveljini.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">A network company of ICICI Venture, Traveljini.com is a travel shop, with information on several Indian destinations, including wildlife sanctuaries. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">World Law - India - Environment</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://http://www.austlii.edu.au/links/50161.html" target="_blank" class="morelink">http://www.austlii.edu.au/links/50161.html</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">World Law is a global catalog and search engine for law and provides a well-organised and searchable index of legal web sites. 
</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Delhibird</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.delhibird.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.delhibird.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Northern India Bird Network offers sites guides, checklists, recent sightings, photogallery and even helps amateurs to identify birds.  </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Janmanch - People's Forum</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.janmanch.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.janmanch.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Janmanch.org is an information exchange platform of CREDO, which provides an extensive resource database as well as opinions and features on development issues. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">CorpWatch India</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.corpwatchindia.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.corpwatchindia.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">CorpWatch India is a platform for Indian movements resisting corporate globalisation to articulate their demands. Provides timely information on Indian struggles, linking them with campaigns worldwide. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">IndianJungles.com</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.indianjungles.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.indianjungles.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">IndianJungles.com is an informed forum for those interested in Indian wildlife. Features news, casefiles and analyses by Nirmal Ghosh, an experienced wildlifer.  </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Naturenet</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.naturenet.net" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.naturenet.net</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">UK-based Naturenet is a voluntary enterprise to provide a good resource for practical nature conservation and countryside management.  </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Earthjustice</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.earthjustice.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.earthjustice.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Earthjustice is a public interest law firm 
dedicated to enforcing and strengthening environmental laws on behalf of organisations and communities to protect the earth and defend the right of all people to a healthy environment. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">National Audubon Society</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.audubon.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.audubon.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The National Audubon Society, founded in 1905, works to conserve and restore natural ecosystems, focusing on birds and other wildlife for the benefit of humanity and the earth's biological diversity. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Earth First! Journal</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.earthfirstjournal.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.earthfirstjournal.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Earth First! is an international movement composed of small, bioregionally-based groups who work to protect local ecology through education, litigation, and creative civil disobedience. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Sierra Club</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.sierraclub.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.sierraclub.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Founded in 1892, Sierra Club's grassroots advocacy makes it one of America's most influential environmental organisations. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">The Ocean Conservancy</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.oceanconservancy.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.oceanconservancy.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Ocean Conservancy works to protect ocean ecosystems and conserve the global abundance and diversity of marine wildlife through science-based advocacy, research and public education. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Center for Health, Environment and Justice</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.chej.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.chej.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">US-based Center for Health Environment and Justice, works by community empowerment at the grassroots to ensure environmental justice. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Optics for Birding</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.optics4birding.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.optics4birding.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Optics4birding is designed to educate birders who want to buy optics (binoculars and telescopes, primarily) so that they can make informed buying decisions. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Indian Mangroves</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.mangroveindia.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.mangroveindia.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Indian Mangroves provides information on the ecological status of mangroves, conservation measures and research projects. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.ipcc.ch" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.ipcc.ch</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The role of the IPCC is to assess the scientific, technical and socio-economic information relevant for the understanding of the risk of human-induced climate change. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Environmental Investigation Agency</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.eia-international.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.eia-international.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Environmental Investigation Agency is an independent, international campaigning organisation committed to investigating and exposing environmental crime. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Hornocker Wildlife Institute</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.hwi.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.hwi.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Hornocker Wildlife Institute, a programme of the Wildlife Conservation Society, uses hands-on field research to promote a balance between man and nature. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Defenders of Wildlife</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.defenders.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.defenders.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Defenders of Wildlife is dedicated to the protection of all native species in their natural communities, with focus on the accelerating rate of extinction and the associated loss of biodiversity, habitat alteration and destruction. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Earth Island Institute</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.earthisland.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.earthisland.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Earth Island Institute develops and supports projects that counteract threats to the biological and cultural diversity that sustain the environment. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">The Nature Conservancy</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://nature.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">nature.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Nature Conservancy is working to preserve the plants, animals and natural communities that represent the diversity of life on Earth by protecting the lands and waters they need to survive. Saving the last great places... 
</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Worldwatch Institute</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.worldwatch.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.worldwatch.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Worldwatch is dedicated to informing policymakers and the public about emerging global problems and trends and the complex links between the world economy and its environmental support systems. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">In Defense of Animals</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.idausa.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.idausa.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">IDA works to protect the rights, welfare and habitats of animals and to end their exploitation and abuse. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">50 years is enough!</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.50years.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.50years.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The US network for global economic justice is a coalition of organisations dedicated to the transformation of the World Bank and the IMF through action-oriented economic literacy training, public mobilisation, and policy advocacy. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Wildlife Conservation Society</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://wcs.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">wcs.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Wildlife Conservation Society is a US-based organization managing national and international conservation projects, research and education programs. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Project Tiger</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://envfor.nic.in/pt/pt.html" target="_blank" class="morelink">envfor.nic.in/pt/pt.html</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Project Tiger was launched on April 1, 1973 in Corbett on the basis of the recommendations of a special task-force of the Indian Board of Wildlife. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Greenpeace India</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.greenpeaceindia.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.greenpeaceindia.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Greenpeace India chapter has been working with local groups investigating and exposing instances of toxic trade, hazardous waste dumping and toxic pollution. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">International Crane Foundation</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.savingcranes.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.savingcranes.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The International Crane Foundation works worldwide to conserve cranes and the wetland and grasslands communities on which they depend. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Discovery</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.discovery.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.discovery.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Discovery Communications is packed with interactive learning channels. Live-cams, e-cards, games... </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Natural Resources Defense Council</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.nrdc.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.nrdc.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Natural Resources Defense Council, with a membership base of over 40,000, uses legislation and policy to conserve and protect the earth's resources. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Pew Center on Global Climate Change</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://pewclimate.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">pewclimate.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Pew Center on Global Climate Change is dedicated to providing credible information, straight answers and innovative solutions to address global climate change. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">TRAFFIC</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.traffic.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.traffic.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">TRAFFIC, the wildlife trade monitoring network, works to ensure that trade in wild plants and animals is not a threat to the conservation of nature. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://sdnp.delhi.nic.in/nbsap/" target="_blank" class="morelink">sdnp.delhi.nic.in/nbsap/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The National Policy and Macrolevel Action Strategy on Biodiversity by the MoEF is a macro-level statement of policies, gaps and strategies needed for conservation and sustainable use of biological diversity. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Birdlife International</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.birdlife.net" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.birdlife.net</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Birdlife International is a global alliance of national conservation organisations working in more than 100 countries worldwide, to identify, monitor and protect Important Birding Areas. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">PETA India</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.petaindia.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.petaindia.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Based in Mumbai, PETA India operates under the simple principle that animals are not ours to eat, wear, experiment on or use for entertainment. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">5tigers: Tiger Information Centre</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.5tigers.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.5tigers.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The site is a must for anyone who wants to know more about tigers. It allows access to vital comtemporary data about tigers and their habitats. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">IUCN</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.iucn.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.iucn.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The World Conservation Union was founded in 1948 and the IUCN has helped over 75 countries to prepare and implement conservation and biodiversity strategies. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Ministry of Environment and Forests</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://envfor.nic.in" target="_blank" class="morelink">envfor.nic.in</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The official website of the Ministry of Environment and Forests gives the latest information on reports, plans, meetings and environmental clearances. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">OneWorld</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.oneworld.net" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.oneworld.net</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">OneWorld is a community of over 1000 organisations working for social justice. It is part of a very credible and effective initiative that involves research as well as environmental campaigning. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">International Rivers Network</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.irn.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.irn.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">IRN supports local communities working to protect their rivers and watersheds. They work to halt destructive river development projects, and to encourage equitable and sustainable methods of meeting needs for water, energy. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">International Snow Leopard Trust</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.snowleopard.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.snowleopard.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Dedicated to the conservation of the endangered snow leopard and its mountain ecosystem through a balanced approach that considers people and the environment. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Greenpeace</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.greenpeace.org/" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.greenpeace.org/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Greenpeace is an independent, non-political, international organisation that has been fighting for the protection of the environment by peaceful means for several decades now. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Environmental News Network</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.enn.com/" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.enn.com/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">ENN offers educational interactivity with the latest environmental news, features, special reports... and allows an opportunity to interact with others. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">West Bengal Wildlife Wing</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.westbengal.com/wildlife/" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.westbengal.com/wildlife/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Official information from the Directorate of Forests, Government of West Bengal about the state's flora and fauna, wildlife sanctuaries and national parks. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Rainforest Action Network</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.ran.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.ran.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Rainforest Action Network has been working to protect tropical rainforests and the human rights of those living in and around these forests and bring their plight to public attention through education and direct action. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Rajaji National Park</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.rajajinationalpark.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.rajajinationalpark.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Created by the former Field Director of the Park, the site provides information on everything from places of interest to accomodation, tariffs and booking procedures for tourists. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">National Geographic</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.nationalgeographic.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.nationalgeographic.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">They helped Richard Byrd fly over the South Pole, Jane Goodall study chimps and Bob Ballard find the Titanic... The National Geographic Society is the world&#8217;s largest nonprofit scientific and educational organization. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Bombay Natural History Society</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.bnhs.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.bnhs.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Established in 1883, the BNHS plays a vital role in documenting and conserving India's natural heritage. The site details the Society's conservation activities and research projects. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">eNature.com</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.enature.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.enature.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">eNature.com has a database of 4,800 species of plants and animals with colour photographs, online field guides and help with identification. Send wildlife postcards, listen to bird songs, talk to other nature enthusiasts. eNature's content is derived from the best-selling National Audubon Society Field Guide series. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">The Thousand Tigers Website</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.web.net/~pcarter/hazaribagh/" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.web.net/~pcarter/hazaribagh/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Maintained by Philip Carter, a Canadian writer who travelled to Bihar in 1997, the site focusses on Hazaribagh, a town near the North Karanpura valley, famed as the 'land of a thousand tigers' and now under threat from several mining projects. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">The Ecologist</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.theecologist.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.theecologist.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Founded in 1970 and read in over 150 countries, <i>The Ecologist</i> is an environmental magazine that has been opening new areas of debate on science and technology to the impact of globalisation on economic development. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Madhya Pradesh Forest Department</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.madhyapradeshforest.org/htmlfiles/wildlife.html" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.madhyapradeshforest.org/htmlfiles/wildlife.html</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">With wilderness areas such as the Kanha Tiger Reserve, Pench Tiger Reserve, Bandhavgarh Tiger Reserve and other protected areas, Madhya Pradesh is home to some of the country's best forests and wildlife. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Corporate Watch</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.corporatewatch.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.corporatewatch.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Corporate Watch is a radical research and publishing group based in the United Kingdom that was set up to support activism against large corporations. Often stepping into controversial areas, the group pushes hard to obtain corporate accountability. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">People's Commission on Environment and Development</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.pcedindia.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.pcedindia.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">PCED, an NGO launched in New Delhi in 1990, holds public hearings in the country on environmental and development issues to induce the people to dialogue with government about critical issues. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Essential Information - Encouraging Activism</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.essential.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.essential.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Founded in 1982 by Ralph Nader, Essential Information is a non-profit organization involved in a variety of projects to encourage citizens to become active and engaged in their communities. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Maharashtra Forest Department</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.mahaforest.gov.in" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.mahaforest.gov.in</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The official site of the Maharashtra Forest Department offers tourism and biodiversity information on the tiger haunts of Gugamal, Tadoba and Pench as well as Borivli and Navegaon National Park, alongwith maps. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Wild Ventures</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.wildventures.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.wildventures.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Wild Ventures is a site that promotes eco-tourism in India's wilderness areas. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">International Wolf Center</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.wolf.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.wolf.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The International Wolf Centre supports the survival of the wolf globally by teaching about its life, its association with other species and its dynamic relationships to humans. 
</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Whale and Dolphin Conservation Society</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.wdcs.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.wdcs.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The global voice for the protection of whales, dolphins and their environment. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Wildlife Trust of India</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.wildlifetrustofindia.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.wildlifetrustofindia.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Wildlife Trust of India is a conservation organisation, committed to crisis management and the provision of quick, efficient aid. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Mountain Forum</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.mtnforum.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.mtnforum.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Mountain Forum is a network empowering mountain supporters by providing an opportunity to share lessons from the field, and bring these into policy discussions. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Nepal's Department of Wildlife and Forest Conservation</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://http://www.south-asia.com/dnpwc/intro.htm" target="_blank" class="morelink">http://www.south-asia.com/dnpwc/intro.htm</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Department works to conserve and manage the wildlife heritage of the mountain kingdom of Nepal. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Crocodilians - Natural History and Conservation</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.crocodilian.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.crocodilian.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The crocodile site with information on different species, their biology and conservation, how they talk, and even their captive care. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">True Food Network</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.truefoodnow.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.truefoodnow.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The True Food Network is a free service from Greenpeace, to connect consumers who want to take action to end the use of genetically engineered ingredients in our foods. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">American Journal of Botany</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.amjbot.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.amjbot.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Covers research on all aspects of plant biology - from plant morphology and palaeobotany to genetics and molecular biology. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Alameda County Waste Management Authority</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.stopwaste.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.stopwaste.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Run by a local county government in California, this is exemplary of community action in the neighbourhood advocating recycling measures. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Wildlife Heritage Trust of Sri Lanka</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.wht.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.wht.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">WHT is a non-profit organization which serves primarily a vehicle for biodiversity exploration, research and direct conservation activity. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Endangered Species Coalition</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.stopextinction.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.stopextinction.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">US-based oragnisation that advocates the use of education, scientific information and public participation in decisions affecting the fate of threatened and endangered species. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Journal of International Wildlife Law and Policy</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.jiwlp.com" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.jiwlp.com</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Journal addresses legal and political issues concerning the human race's interrelationship with and management of wildlife species, their habitats, and the biosphere. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">World Commission on Dams</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.dams.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.dams.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The World Commission on Dams is a focussed, independent think tank set up to look at the good, the bad and the ugly impacts of dams around the world. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">UNEP World Conservation Monitoring Centre</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.unep-wcmc.org/" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.unep-wcmc.org/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The site provides information for policy and action to conserve the living world. Their programmes concentrate on species, forests, protected areas and other aspects of biodiversity assessment. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Food and Agriculture Organisation</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.fao.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.fao.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The website of the UN FAO provides useful statistics on production, trade, food balance sheets, land use and irrigation, forest and fishery products etc. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">World Bank</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.worldbank.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.worldbank.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Check this site to keep aware of various projects that the organisation is involved in, the latest reports and their operations and policies. Read between the lines... </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">World Resources Institute</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.wri.org/" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.wri.org/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">An environmental information portal, WRI's mission is to move human society to live in ways that protect Earth&#8217;s environment for current and future generations. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Exxon Valdez: Legacy of an oil spill</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.oilspill.state.ak.us" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.oilspill.state.ak.us</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">This site, by the Exxon Valdez Oil Spill Trustee Council, provides information about the impacts of the oil spill, the injury and recovery of fish, wildlife, and people.  </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">World Wildlife Fund</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.worldwildlife.org/" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.worldwildlife.org/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Known worldwide by its panda logo, WWF is a premier conservation organisation dealing with environmental protection and development-related issues. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Wildlife Institute of India</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.wii.gov.in" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.wii.gov.in</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">WII research projects are conducted across the country and are the primary source of scientific data to aid conservation. With access to papers and articles, it is a useful site to learn about training programmes. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Conservation International</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.conservation.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.conservation.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Conservation International uses science, economics, policy and community involvement to promote biodiversity and conservation in tropical rainforests and other endangered ecosystems worldwide. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">CITES</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.cites.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.cites.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">The Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES) came into force on July 1, 1975 to help curb the wildlife trade and help protect species against exploitation for trade. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Institute for Global Communications - EcoNet</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.igc.org/igc/gateway/enindex.html" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.igc.org/igc/gateway/enindex.html</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">EcoNet was the world's first computer network dedicated to environmental preservation and sustainability. IGC strategically uses technology to enable international co-operation on issues. </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Vanashakti</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.vanashakti.in" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.vanashakti.in</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Vanashakti is founded by ordinary folk who want to do something for India & Indians. We believe that middle class India has to play a role in ensuring proper governance. For too long we have sat back and complained about the deterioration in the world around us. We need to make people aware that they have a stake in the world around them.</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Save the Rani Bagh</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://www.saveranibagh.org" target="_blank" class="morelink">www.saveranibagh.org</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">Alarmed at the recently publicized plans for the so-called makeover of Jijamata Udyan, Mumbai better known as Rani Bagh we, a group of Mumbai citizens and nature lovers, have formed an action committee to create awareness and oppose the proposed plans of the Brihamumbai Municipal Corporation (BMC) to convert a green haven into a concrete amusement park as per a Rs.433 crore contract with HKS Designer and Consultant International (a Thai-based Malaysian company) and the Portico Group (US). </td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="subhead">Vet Education</td></tr><tr><td><a href = "http://http://www.veteducation.com.au/" target="_blank" class="morelink">http://www.veteducation.com.au/</a></td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr><tr><td class="articletext">At veteducation.com.au, our mission is to provide you with practical, relevant distance learning of the highest standards. The directors of veteducation.com.au, Philip and Charisma Judge, are dedicated to providing you with continuing education opportunities that present the most up-to-date knowledge, delivered to you by experienced veterinarians, who have a passion for teaching.</td></tr><tr><td class="commontext"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="10" height="10"></td></tr>
            </table>

            <p>&nbsp;</p>

            <!-- #EndEditable --></td>
          <td width="7%" valign="top"><img src="../sanctuaryimages/blank.gif" width="20" height="10"></td>
